---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout title="About — Rithvik A Koundinya" description="About Rithvik A Koundinya and the dot.">
  <section class="page-section container container--narrow">
    <h1 class="page-title">About the dot</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        In my name — <strong>Ṛithvik</strong> — there is a dot under the R.
        It's a small mark, easy to miss. But it's part of who I am, and it became the idea behind this portfolio.
      </p>

      <p>
        A dot is a beginning. A full stop. A point on a timeline. In design, it's the smallest unit that still
        carries meaning — a shape, a pause, a place to rest your eye.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm a designer drawn to how forms carry feeling — whether that's the emotional language of shape in
        horology, the negative space between letterforms on a folded brochure, or the interaction that welcomes
        someone at a conference booth.
      </p>

      <p>
        This site is project-based because that's how I think: each piece of work is a story with a beginning,
        a turn, and something that lingers. I hope it feels warm here. Pull up a chair.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-actions">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--accent">Say hello</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
